    "note": "Statement of record: gate 5 grades the constants the driver PRINTS, not the ones it USES; and the zero branch is tested before the luna88k branch, so BUDGET=0 prints a green row while removing the only work ceiling. MANUAL - the mutants are predicted, not executed, so build them and watch the rows stay green BEFORE repairing. R3 RESEARCH CLOSURE: the hole is OBSERVED (both mutants green, literal lines banked). THE MAJORITY DESIGN IS REFUTED - shared locals cannot kill an argument-expression mutant, because a local proves what the caller INTENDED to pass, not what the callee RECEIVED. Chosen: record the callee's formal parameters and print those; order the calibrated-rig case first and make it RED; factor the classifier into lib.sh so the branch is reachable offline; and ship a STRADDLE detector that reads the printed budget from the driver's own output and proves N-1 does not stop while N+1 does."
