  {
   "id": "b115",
   "title": "#115  Read path: an unaligned overlay read takes bytes from the wrong layer; a short flat-CD read loses data",
   "state": "held",
   "commits": "00d546d",
   "closure": {
    "by": "fable5",
    "badge": "",
    "note": "Statement of record: the overlay read loop neither clamps the read to the block remainder nor advances the buffer by the amount read, so an unaligned read takes bytes from the wrong layer AND duplicates them - measured, 1022 of 1024 bytes wrong - while returning the FULL length, so every caller check is bypassed. Overlays are the normal rig case. The CD half reports all-zeros as GOOD. CONFIRMED. Constraint: keep #416's advertised-gap contract."
   },
   "entries": [
    {
     "seat": "kimi",
     "phase": "assess",
     "d": "✓",
