   "state_note": "*** REFUTED 2026-08-27 and DROPPED. Stale row: the defect was real and was FIXED by `#432`. ***\n\nThe row says the legal `TIMER_EXTERNAL` clock value stops the emulator. **`dev_footbridge.c` handles that encoding explicitly and no longer exits**, and the code says so in its own comment at the `TIMER_1_CONTROL` write arm:\n  > *\"#432: both prescaler bits set is TIMER_EXTERNAL (0x0C, dc21285reg.h:364) -- a LEGAL named encoding, and it used to reach fatal()+exit(1) right here, so a guest selecting the external clock source KILLED THE HOST. ... footbridge_effective_cycles() now gives the encoding a defined, survivable meaning (the unprescaled period), and the real semantics are filed for a round that has a datasheet.\"*\n\n**Verified independently of the seat**: that comment was read directly during this session's work on a DIFFERENT row in the same file, before this brief was answered. Two readings, same conclusion.\n\nThe seat adds that regression row C1 already covers the encoding, so the defence is not merely the fix but a pinned row.\n\n*Historically guest-reachable on CATS/NetWinder -- the row was true when filed. This is the fifth row today found to describe work already done; see [[baretitle]].*\n\n"
