     "note": "FLAGSHIP ADJUDICATION, queue item 7, batched. Badge `s` disclosed: same-model review of the main loop's records, not a two-family check. Re-verified every code claim by grep/read; boots and mutant builds attributed to the measure seat rather than re-run.\n* *** THE FINDING IS A FLAW IN THE LADDER IT WROTE THIS MORNING: THE RUNG ORDER AND THE PRIORITY ORDER DIVERGE. *** b120r's witness is rung 4 (an instrumented boot) while armbdt's is rung 3 (a probe), so the ladder's clause 'order items by the strongest witness that exists TODAY' puts b120r FIRST. That is wrong for scheduling: b120r's measured guest-visible symptom is NIL (told-98 and told-35 give byte-identical transcripts) while armbdt CORRUPTS GUEST DATA. RUNG MEASURES REACHABILITY-PROOF STRENGTH, NOT HARM. The carrier clause is corrected.\nCONFIRM: TRUE as code, DEAD as defect. Drop as a round, rider on the next diskimage round. READ-verified exactly TWO call sites, emul_parse.c:558 and main.c:707, both branching on < 0 and both aborting. Nothing consumes a half-built entry, so no execution witness exists OR IS NEEDED -- rung-none by construction. Re-promote only if a third, non-aborting caller appears."
