     "verdict": "REAL",
     "evidence": "MANUAL",
     "note": "*** THIRD FILE-READING SEAT TO REFUTE THE DUPLICATE SUSPICION, independently: 'b120r is a distinct residual, not a duplicate of #281/#286' and 'do not drop b120r'. *** agy, grok and opus5 all read the code and all three agree; the two packet seats that voted DROP could not check and sided with the brief's own suspicion. On repo fact the reading seats win, and this is now 3-0 among seats that could actually look.  [panel_20260817_174701]"
    },
    {
     "phase": "research",
     "seat": "opus5",
     "date": "2026-08-19",
     "verdict": "REAL",
     "evidence": "CONFIRMED",
     "note": "*** MEASURED ACROSS THREE GUESTS AND FIVE INSTRUMENTED ARMS. The lie is real, it REACHES the guest, the guest DOES read the field -- and on the shipping value no guest on any rig is harmed. Priority drops; the fix does not become unnecessary. ***\n* TRAFFIC: pmax/OpenBSD 2.2 (old-style rz driver) issues ZERO MODE SENSE across a full multiuser boot plus disklabel, mount and raw dd -- a clean negative. arc/OpenBSD 2.2 issues 5x MODE SENSE(6) page 4: asked 32, got 32, TOLD 132, true 36. That reproduces the brief's capture exactly. luna88k/OpenBSD 7.7 issues 11x across pages 0/4/8: asked 254, got 254, TOLD 98.\n* *** THE WRAP IS ALREADY EXERCISED IN NORMAL OPERATION: luna88k asks 254, so 254+100=354 WRAPS to 98. *** It merely lands on a value the guest tolerates. Measured sweep: reported==0 at exactly alloc==156, and reported < true-1 for alloc in [156,190]. No rig asks 156, so the defect is ONE allocation-length change away from the arm-C behaviour below, not a hypothetical.\n* THE CHANNEL IS LIVE, proved by a POSITIVE CONTROL rather than assumed: sending cyl=1234/heads=9 changes arc's attach line from '2081 cyl, 16 head, 63 sec' to '1234 cyl, 9 head, 188 sec'. The response body IS consumed.\n* AND IT REFUTED ITS OWN DRAFT: it had written that a page-4 rpm change proves consumption; arm D showed disklabel still printed 3600 because that value comes from the ON-DISK LABEL, not from MODE SENSE. The control killed its own claim before it shipped.\n* HARM, MEASURED: luna88k told-98 vs told-35/11 produce ORDERED TRANSCRIPTS IDENTICAL, 0 diff lines across 97 lines each. But told-0 FLIPS CONTROL FLOW -- 32 MODE SENSE instead of 11, including MODE SENSE(10) fallbacks and page 5. OpenBSD 7.7 branches on this byte. So 98 and 132 sit in a tolerated 'nonzero and >= true' region; 0 does not.\n* *** THE OBVIOUS FIX IS WRONG: `retlen -= 100` writes the ALLOCATION LENGTH. *** The spec wants true_len-1, measured as 11/23/35/35/43 for pages 0/1/3/4/5 -- the allocation length is correct only by coincidence at alloc==191. The true value is not known at :607 because the page is written later at :630+, so the write must MOVE AFTER the pagecode switch.\n* BLAST RADIUS: nothing reads retlen after :607 (next use :746 is an assignment in the READ case), and data_in[0] is read NOWHERE outside diskimage_scsicmd.c across all of src/ -- every HBA sizes from data_in_len, so the guest is the only consumer. No overflow: max write is q+29 = 45 against a >=100-byte buffer.\n* DETECTOR built and feasible offline. TWO DESIGN POINTS THAT MATTER: the rows MUST SPAN PAGES {0,1,3,4,5}, because every page-4 case has true_len 36 and a mutant hardcoding 35 would pass a page-4-only test; and an INVARIANCE row -- the reported length must not vary with the allocation length -- NAMES THE DEFECT RATHER THAN A VALUE, so a '+100 -> +0' half-fix cannot pass it. -ffunction-sections/-Wl,--gc-sections is required or mymkstemp/debug_indentation fail to link.\n* ADJACENT, measured en route: MODE SENSE(10) writes the 6-BYTE header layout, so a conformant guest parses block_desc_len=0 while 8 real descriptor bytes sit at offset 8 -- STRICTLY WORSE than b120r, and unreached today only because no rig issues MS10. And data_in_len is set to the FULL allocation length even when far less data exists (alloc 255 -> 255 bytes, 219 of them zeros) where a real drive transfers 36, which affects residual logic.\n* HONEST UNKNOWN, stated by the seat: three guests measured, ALL OpenBSD. Whether a NetBSD/Ultrix/Linux driver asks an allocation length in [156,190] was not measured.\n* It also caught a citation error of mine: REQUEST SENSE forcing is :964-967, not the :957-960 my brief claimed. Verified and corrected above.  [agent b120r 2026-08-19]"
    },
    {
     "phase": "assess",
