     "note": "FABLE REGRESS ADJUDICATION of verdict_20260819_135703 at 6014b7e. Badge `s` disclosed: same-model adjudication of the main loop's records, not a two-family check.\n* *** Q2 REFUTED MY OWN SUSPICION USING THE BATTERY'S OWN LOG. *** I wrote that no gate asserts the guest-visible CHECK CONDITION. Lines 554 and 559 say otherwise (verified here): `overlay: a failed sync reports CHECK CONDITION 2` and `nothing open: sync reports CHECK CONDITION, not GOOD 2` -- FAULT-INJECTED via fail_fsync_fd returning EIO, driven through the real diskimage_scsicommand() with a WRITE(10)-then-SYNCHRONIZE-CACHE CDB pair, not a direct call. So gate 2 EXERCISED the changed path discriminatingly rather than merely not breaking on it. The live gates ran the success leg for real: luna88k reached login in gates 5 and 7.\n* Q1 MY FRAMING WAS WRONG IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. Too strong: the battery is NOT the evidence the harness commits did not break the emulator -- GIT IS. `git diff --name-only 1ba2cd4..6014b7e` minus regress/tools/docs leaves exactly the three #437 files, so no build input outside #437 changed and the harness commits COULD NOT have altered the binary. Too weak: the 16/16 IS evidence about those commits -- it is the first end-to-end execution of their product, 16/16 with 0 skipped means no gate silently dropped out, and the selfmutant controls DETECTED in this run.\n* AND A FRAMING ERROR I REPEATED TWICE TODAY: diskimage_sync() does NOT sit on a path 'every rig's disk traffic crosses'. ONLY command 0x35 reaches it; ordinary READ/WRITE cross diskimage_scsicommand() but not the sync handler. The blast radius is narrower than I said.\n* #437 touched THREE src/ files, not one: diskimage.c, diskimage_scsicmd.c, diskimage.h. 'One src/ COMMIT' was true; the round record should name the three files.\n* Q3 NO EMERGENCY RE-RUN for 20ce22e and 7e3b120 -- every changed line is gate 2's surface or non-battery tooling, and the binary is bit-identical by construction, so a full battery 