    "note": "Measured during R3's review, and recorded so the record does not read as fuller coverage than exists. The straddle does NOT catch: (1) a mutant that scales BOTH the print and the comparison - only the literal config-pin row catches that, which is why both row kinds stay; (2) an in-body change to STALL or BACKSTOP, because nothing straddles either and the under-leg accepts BACKSTOP as a stated reason; (3) `>` changed to `>=` at the comparison, which scores zero red rows. An in-body budget change is caught only to within one instruction. Closing (2) needs a stall/backstop straddle of the same shape.  closure.by normalised 2026-08-25 from 'opus' to 'opus5' -- the ledger's declared roster has opus5 and no 'opus'; a one-row spelling variant that every non-empty check passes."
