     "note": "*** VERDICT: THE FILE IS THE WRONG UNIT -- MEASURED, NOT ARGUED. Close as documented-only with the census as the standing answer. *** **91% IS THE KILLER:** of 118 `.c` files in src/devices/, **107 carry at least one terminating site** -- so a per-file 'stops the host' flag marks 91% of the population, because CHECK_ALLOCATION at init is near-universal (144 of 183 macro sites are INIT, and INIT is 47% of the whole tally). **A metric that flags 91% of its population ranks nothing and schedules nothing.** Only **29** files carry an ACCESS site at all, so 78 of those listed are permanently zero in the only bucket that matters. Even within ACCESS the distribution defeats per-file completeness: top 5 files are 54%, median 2, and 13 of 29 have exactly one. **THE QUEUE HAS CONFUSED THESE DENOMINATORS MORE THAN THE BRIEF ADMITTED:** it traced 114 -> 170 -> 220 -> 253/271 -> 360 across the record, with devexit's own closure note carrying two different universes in one sentence AND the warning 'RECORD THE UNIVERSE OR THE NUMBER LOOKS WRONG LATER'. The brief said 'confused once'; it is at least three times. THE THREE UNITS, and only two are needed: **FILE is a SCHEDULING unit and never a coverage denominator**; **guest-reachable ACCESS SITE (90) is the ELIGIBILITY denominator** -- with the caveat that even ACCESS contains known non-defects (dev_cons.c:80's intended exit(0), dev_ram.c:132's guest-unreachable mode), so 90 is eligibility and not a defect count; and **DE-FATALISED PREDICATE is the OBLIGATION denominator**, the only one that maps onto existing machinery (accept rows and clause (d) are both per-predicate). *** THE RECORD THE ROW ASKS FOR ALREADY EXISTS, PER-SITE, IN THE SOURCE: 51 sites across 12 files already carry a `/* #NNN: was exit(1) */` tag *** -- dev_pvr.c 25, gdrom 5, osiop 5, 8253 4, pcc2 4, and seven more. That is more precise than the per-file tally requested, written at the site, keyed by round, in the fork's own tagging ethos. Combined with `census_exits.py --by-file`, which ships and the seat ran, both halves are satisfied. BOUNDED RESIDUAL: nothing answers 'of the 90 ACCESS sites, which already carry a tag?' -- a one-flag addition (`--tagged`), discharged once, not a standing policy. CONSTRAINT ON THE PREDICATE UNIT, measured and limiting: **the latch idiom is not uniform** -- at least four spellings coexist (struct `warned_*`, function-local `static int warned`, `static int w_warned/r_warned`, and others) -- so a predicate census needs the idiom normalised first, which is separate work and must not be smuggled in."
