wdcidentorder open low wdcidentorder  harness: swapping the two IDENTIFY transmit pushes byte-swaps every word the guest reads at ZERO differential failures -- the differential reads identify_struct directly; `row_command_fills_ring' checks occupancy (512), not bytes; the detector header said 'so it is filed' from #405 on with no row behind it
wdcstubtype open low wdcstubtype  harness: the wdc differential's disk stubs ignore the bus `type' argument ((void) type in diskimage_exist/diskimage_access), so a wrong bus-type argument at the three call sites escapes
wdcgeomparse open low wdcgeomparse  harness: the geometry differential's -ULLONG_MAX row covers the SPT position only, so a strtoll -> strtoull change at the HEADS parse site escapes
lbsmask open low lbsmask  diskimage.c: `size & (logical_block_size - 1)' assumes a power-of-two block size at >= 3 sites (the #414 block names them); the vector is held behind `#ifdef GEOM_ROW_LBS257' in diff_diskimage_geom.c and was disclosed but never filed
wdcfloodprobe open low wdcfloodprobe  harness: the #464 flood probe's `print r3' 'completion control' is printed and never parsed by any row; its `fire3' row comment claims every period N > 1 (it covers 2 and 3); its header says every row single-steps (false since #486's free-running runloop); the gate's fatal-call floor (>= 12) tolerates one fatal -> debug downgrade at HEAD's 13 sites
wdcdiagerr open low wdcdiagerr  after EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC (and after a channel reset) dev_wdc.c sets `d->error = 1' -- the correct error-REGISTER diagnostic code (01h = no error detected) -- but `status_byte' ORs WDCS_ERR whenever d->error != 0, so the STATUS register shows ERR while the error register says 'no error'; upstream code
m88kdslotshadow open med m88kdslotshadow  cpu_m88k.c: for a precise fault in the delay slot of a taken br.n the else-arm sets SNIP = slot+4, SFIP = target (upstream's 'Perhaps something like this could work'); the MC88100 UM says the shadows copy NIP = target, FIP = target+4 -- rte then executes slot+4 (skipped by the branch) before the target, or the target twice when target == slot+4
