ent defect in the tree ***", "hold": null}, {"id": "alphaintdeliver", "state": "open", "sev": "med", "title": "Alpha has NO interrupt delivery -- #516's decline is the disposition, this is the SUBSYSTEM it declines into.  cd.alpha.irq_asserted is written (cpu_alpha.c:218,:223) and read nowhere; cpu_dyntrans.c delivers for FIVE architectures and has no Alpha arm; memory_rw.c's failed-device branch dispatches only for MIPS and M88K.  Implementing it is dyntrans dispatch + PALcode entry + the IPL check -- its own round.  NOT a host-kill and lower than the kills it grew from: Alpha interrupts have never worked on this tree, #516 only stopped the host dying.  No guest that NEEDS delivery has been measured; the row claims the mechanism is absent, not that a guest is blocked.", "hold": null}, {"id": "wdcsingleleg", "state": "open", "sev": "med", "title": "wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py -- a single-leg mode plus a pass/fail contract for the ONE WDC two-leg differential that is genuinely infrastructure-blocked: it imports none of wdc_altoffset_probe, carries its own pty/Emu, ties its expectations to DISK CONTENT (needs a POISONED image the battery does not build), and adds an endianness axis (-e maltabe).  RETITLED 2026-09-09 from 'all four WDC differentials': the other three are one instrument (`import wdc_altoffset_probe as W') and belong to `wdcaltoffleg'.  Its wiringcliff exemption is re-dated naming THIS row and DELETED in the same edit as its wiring when this ships.", "hold": null}, {"id": "alphaswpctxmut", "state": "open", "sev": "low", "title": "alphaswpctxreg (#514, 3031a30) shipped with clause (d) 'satisfied by construction' -- an ARGUMENT, not a built mutant.  Build it: publish the NEW context in v0 instead of the OLD (the incorrect repair the three-value oracle C/N/S was designed against) and measure regress/alpha_swpctx_v0_probe.py against it.  Late-dissent disposition 2: a measured-false-pass check on a shipped detector, one build.", "hold": null}, {"id": "wdcaltoffleg", "state": "open", "sev": "med", "title": "The THREE altoffset WDC differentials as ONE instrument -- wdc_altoffset_probe.py and the two that `import wdc_altoffset_probe as W' (_sig, _4bit): one module, one rig (-E evbmips -e malta, the battery's own _images/wdc-scratch-64m.img), one media family (the `c' in ciR: is a PREFIX -- MEASURED, the same image attaches as an IDE CD-ROM).  OWED: (a) the parent's `ok' -- already a complete verdict over 18 explicit expectations -- gets an exit status, FIRST QUESTION being whether a nonzero exit breaks the two-leg driver; (b) _4bit's single-leg form is an ORACLE CHOICE (its verdict is definitionally between-leg -- 'its whole point is that it DIFFERS by leg', :216), so the round chooses the fix-side absolute and says so; (c) _sig's `sig' oracle is NON-DISCRIMINATING (unreadable and unrelated values both read as 'declined') and is REDESIGNED, not bolted onto.  Each of the three wiringcliff exemptions is re-dated naming THIS row and DELETED in the same edit as its wiring.", "hold": null}, {"id": "witnessclassdoor", "state": "open", "sev": "med", "title": "check_probe_wiring.py: CLASSIFICATION decides whether an un-gated probe's debt is VISIBLE -- an un-gated CLASS_DETECTOR is UNWIRED (fail) or dated EXEMPT, an un-gated CLASS_WITNESS renders `not run (correct)' -- and at least 8 of the 25 CLASS_WITNESS entries describe a POST-FIX-GREEN outcome, which is the checker's own definition of a detector.  So detector debt escapes through the class field, UNDATED, faster than the dated EXEMPT table retires it.  Instance made today: lca_irqstub_probe.py, kept WITNESS 'because re-classing it would demand a gate home'.  Deriver (Opus): the MANIFEST's CLASS_WITNESS entries grepped for 'fix N/M' or 'post-fix green'; 8 of 18 is a FLOOR, one entry unsettled.  Fix shape: a class rule (a witness that has gone post-fix-green IS a detector and owes a gate or a dated exemption) with a dated cutoff -- its own harness round with negative controls, never a rider.  *** COUNT CORRECTED 2026-09-09: the population is 25, not 18 (deriver: an AST extraction of the MANIFEST dict, cross-checked against the checker's own `25 witnesses correctly ungated' line); 8 of 25 carry a post-fix outcome in the note, and wdcnoirq's preserved RESULTS.txt makes a ninth.  The 18 was a seat's floor from a grep and stands demoted here.  The `faster than the EXEMPT table retires it' clause is UNMEASURED. ***", "hold": null}, {"id": "lcairqedgepin", "state": "open", "sev": "low", "title": "lca_irqstub_probe.py: no BASE-RUN row pins the second ISA line's assert EDGE.  `uart live' proves the MCR store landed; on the fix the latched announce prints once whether or not [E] re-entered the stub, so if the UART silently stopped asserting, M12 would escape again and no row would say why.  The measurement-time evidence is M12's own `assert once' = 3 (TABLE_G.out).  A green-run pin needs a different channel: read PIC1's IRR back after [E] and want 0x12.  One row; changes the instrument, so it owes a table.", "hold": null}, {"id": "armbfxcells", "state": "open", "sev": "low", "title": "armbfxwidth32 (c0c7f55 + later rows): FOUR weakening cells named by codex with rows that WOULD kill them and no built mutant -- UBFX full-width relaxed to admit 31; SBFX the same; SBFX width-restriction-on-sign (derived equivalent); SBFX sign-bit requirement dropped.  Build the four and score them; a 'would' is not a measurement.  Also check the shipped handler comments state the width-32 BEHAVIOUR change (L4 if not).", "hold": null}, {"id": "sgimtelabelcells", "state": "in work", "sev": "med", "title": "sgi_mte_fill_probe.py (#509) is BLIND AT TWO OF THREE LABELS: every transfer row drives dst_tlb == MTE_TLB_A, so `if (depth == 32 && dst_tlb == MTE_TLB_A)' and `&& dst_tlb != MTE_TLB_C' each score 14/14 against a 14/14 base (MEASURED, killtable3_20260909/), while a guest-only control shows the CI-arm defect #509 closed LIVE at B and C under them.  RULED FLOOR by 7g-1 (th