ROW lcaisalane in work dev_lca.c DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_isa): THREE defects in eleven lines -- an off-by-one guard that lets a bus-hitting read return all zeros, a discarded downstream failure result, and an uninitialised byte consumed on that failure HOLD None
codex assess Censused the idiom across five files, bounded every severity, found the obvious one-character fix makes things WORSE, and identified a double-count with lcabadval.
codex design GPT-6 Astra @ max, file-reading, the full enclosing function inlined (sketch rule); no refusal.  VERDICT: `ofs >= len' with member 3, and return downstream failure BEFORE packing the byte.  DOMAIN: `p = r >> 5; ofs = p & 3' (incoming address bits 5-6); Alpha's alignment helper does NOT reject misaligned accesses (it calls memory_rw), so the carrier's MIPS 8201->6144 example does not transfer; the sixteen (len, ofs) pairs for len in {1,2,4,8} are tabulated (today (1,2),(1,3),(2,3) end the process; (1,1),(2,2) select data[0] and read zeros), and the memory wrapper's 1024-byte split adds (3,0),(3,3),(5,0),(5,3),(6,3),(7,3) and, for straddling accesses, (6,0),(7,0) -- S3's census was incomplete.  At equality the ternary never evaluates `byte': the equality defect and the failed-byte consumption are DIFFERENT paths.  THE FIX: reject `ofs >= len' before any downstream call, state untouched, return 0 for either direction, announce once per instance on a fresh `warned' bit (bit 8 free) with the decline OUTSIDE the latch condition (`%u'/`%zu'); check the downstream read immediately and return 0 before the packing loop (a zero-filled failure buffer is a failed completion, not a load of zero: the Alpha helper returns before writeback); keep the write arm's immediate return; restructure rather than initialise `byte'.  A `>' -> `>=' alone would EXPAND the termination.  Q3 rows: both equality cases decline with zero downstream calls; a repeated refusal declines twice with one announce; a failing backend leaves a nonzero destination sentinel; a failing backend's distinctive byte never reaches the output.  Q4 witness: a byte access at ISA port bits 5-6 = 2 or 3 (ofs 2/3, len 1) on alphabook1 ends the process today -- rung 3 in the lca_badval_probe.py session shape.
codex design verbatim: 'VERDICT: Support member 3 with `ofs >= len` and failure checked before packing, as a bounded repair to the existing byte-lane contract. Correct the producer domain and detector channels before approving the design: the sixteen cells are incomplete, and guest register preservation cannot detect packing before a failed-read return.'  Read the tree.  Established that the model does NOT use `len' as the downstream transfer size (both calls move exactly one byte; `len' governs the guard, the write-byte selection and the packing only).  Walked HRM Table 6-3 in full and supported a separate `lcaisasize' row. *** THE PRODUCER DOMAIN IS LARGER THAN {1,2,4,8} ***: misaligned Alpha accesses fall back to LS_GENERIC_N and memory_rw splits at MRW_SPLIT_MASK = 0x3ff, so lengths 3,5,6,7 reach the handler and (3,3) is a THIRD false-success cell -- with a boundary walk table.  Also: register preservation is a VACUOUS store-decline channel; the equality WRITES really forward data[0] today.  [PASS 1 on the fix design (brief regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/PASS1_brief_20260910.md).]
grok design verbatim: 'VERDICT: Adopt Codex's candidate.'  Re-derived every premise from the tree rather than the packet (S1, S2, S4, S5, member-5 unavailability, the lane walk).  Found ALPHA_FEATURE_BWX is defined and NEVER READ, so nothing gates the byte ops.  *** IT FOUND THE FACT THAT LATER OVERTURNED THE RULING AND FILED IT AS A NOTE ***: 'Write (1,1) is a behaviour change the title does not mention.  STB to LSR (0x3fd) works on HEAD via `%'.  Member 3 stops it.'  Named eight mutants beyond the brief's six, including the direction-conditioned guard, and showed PHYSICAL is unobservable on this machine (ptbr == 0 identity map).  Its own detector table separated accept, decline and vacuous rows.  [PASS 1 on the fix design (brief regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/PASS1_brief_20260910.md).]
glm design packet-fed.  *** SEAT-FAILURE CLASS 5 (thinking burn) AND ITS RECOVERY, both recorded: *** the first shot returned an EMPTY response beside 120,255 characters of hidden reasoning with done_reason=stop -- the signature this project's carrier says is diagnostic on the empty response, NOT on done_reason.  panel_ollama.py re-fired with think=False and got 112,234 characters back.  The retry answers the questions but never emits a verdict line, so seat_verdicts.py files it as a format miss.  READ for its findings and NOT credited with a verdict: it independently proposed the read-side `i == ofs % len' fold (the member-4 dissent) and named six further mutants (m1..m6).  [PASS 1 on the fix design (brief regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/PASS1_brief_20260910.md).]
deepseek design packet-fed.  verbatim: 'VERDICT: The core defect is real and the candidate fix is sound, but several premises (especially 1(d) register value on Alpha) cannot be settled from the packet.'  Honest about what it could not settle and named the single fact that would settle each.  Contributed the `&& len != 2' exemption mutant.  Rejected member 4 on bounds (data has length len, so data[ofs] at equality is OOB) -- which is the correct objection to the NAIVE accept and is answered by the `% len' fold form.  [PASS 1 on the fix design (brief regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/PASS1_brief_20260910.md).]
minimax design packet-fed.  verbatim: 'VERDICT: The three defects are REAL and CONFIRMED ... the model discarding a<4:3> is FORCED by the sparse window so `lcaisasize' is a phantom row'.  *** THAT CLAIM IS MEASURED FALSE and is recorded as the panel's one wrong finding ***: the window is registered 0x10000 << 5 bytes wide with no alignment restriction and `relative_addr >>= 5' discards bits 4:0, so a guest CAN place a<4:3> and the size bits are thrown away -- refuted by reading the registration, and codex, grok, Opus and Fable all walked the same encodings the other way.  Its accept-side reading of the write arm was right and early.  [PASS 1 on the fix design (brief regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/PASS1_brief_20260910.md).]
kimi design PACKET-FED SUBSTITUTE kimi-k3:cloud; the kimi CLI is on its weekly 403 wall (pass1_20260910/kimi.txt is the 350-byte notice) -- the seat is COVERED, not lost.  It caught the brief's PLANTED-LOOKING wrong premise without being told there was one: the (2,3) write never reaches `data[3 % 2]' because the guard exits first, so the modulo's ONLY live effect is folding ofs == len onto index 0.  It drew the corollary that became the dissent -- the arms are ASYMMETRIC at the equality cells, writes work and reads drop the byte -- and flagged the Table 6-3 byte-enable column as staggered.  [PASS 1 on the fix design (brief regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/PASS1_brief_20260910.md).]
