1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
2: """Round 87's measuring instrument: which legal PowerPC FP encodings stop the emulator.
3: 
4: Prints one line per row:  <name> <got> <want> ok|FAIL
5: then PPC_HALT_CONTROL=OK|DEAD and PPC_HALT_RESULT=<passed>/<total>.
6: gate_ppc_halt.sh does the asserting.
7: 
8: What a halt IS here
9: -------------------
10: `cpu_ppc_instr.c`'s translator ends both floating-point blocks with
11: `default: goto bad;`, and `bad:` is the shared label in `cpu_dyntrans.c` that
12: prints "UNIMPLEMENTED instruction at 0x..." and sets `cpu->running = 0`. So a
13: legal encoding the decoder does not know does not raise a program exception the
14: guest could handle -- it stops the whole emulator. Same class as rounds
15: 70/70B/78/79/80 on other architectures.
16: 
17: How the outcome is classified
18: -----------------------------
19: A halt is read off that message, never off a memory marker. The SuperH sweep
20: (round 80) learned this the hard way: a marker-only classifier cannot tell
21: "the emulator stopped" from "the instruction ran and simply did not reach the
22: store", and after a fix lands it reports every repaired row as still broken.
23: Each row therefore reports one of three named outcomes:
24: 
25:   alive    -- stepped, and the session still answers a dump afterwards
26:   HALTED   -- the dyntrans abort message appeared      <- the defect
27:   DEAD     -- the session stopped answering entirely   <- instrument failure
28: 
29: Row classes
30: -----------
31:   CTRL  -- an instruction the decoder already handled. These are what make a
32:            HALTED verdict mean anything: if a control halts, the rig is broken
33:            (wrong machine, no FP, bad address) and no other row may be
34:            believed. Round 76 shipped a probe with no control and every mask
35:            "halted", including the nine that worked.
36:   FIXED -- halted on the build before #326, must run now. `want` is alive, so
39:            records that with `want` = HALTED rather than omitting it. Two
86: CODE = 0x8000
90: def enc(op, rt=0, ra=0, rb=0, frc=0, xo=0, rc=0):
110: def decode(iw):
126: def run(iword):
131:         os.execvp(BIN, [BIN, "-V", "-E", "macppc", "-e", "g4", "-M", "64",
190:               "step 1"]:
283: def main():
285:           % ("row", "got", "want", "class", "word/fields"))
294:         #  hiding it: `want` is HALTED, so the row passes today and FAILS the
297:         want = "HALTED" if cls == "PEND" else "alive"
298:         ok = (got == want)
305:               % (name, got, want, cls, iword, f["op"], f["xo10"], f["xo5"],

