VERDICT: 1. Maple `MAPLE_DMAADDR` readback; 2. XScale `INTEN` readback; 3. MK48T08 NVRAM boundary.
CODEX_EXITAUDIT_20260910

**Seven entries are ready to file.** The re-derived inventory contains **76 unowned runtime error-exit sites in 24 files**, after accounting for existing ownership, enabled device attachments, and reachability exclusions.

I inspected committed blobs at **`4eac0b1ff822d6f8f4b3d6ea3066adbdab3c0a95`**, using the specified repository. All line numbers below refer to that commit. No builds, emulator executions, regression runs, edits, or patches were performed. Test-carrier assessments are based on source inspection.

The earlier figures reproduce, but their description was wrong: **370 and 240 count `exit(1)`, not every `exit()` call.**

The matching scope is immediate tracked `*.c` files in `src/devices/`, `src/cpus/`, and `src/machines/`. It is not a whole-repository count. I enumerated committed files, removed comments and string/character literals while preserving line positions, then located `\bexit\s*\(`. An independent character-state lexer returned exactly the same call positions. This counts physical source sites without expanding macros or eliminating conditional compilation.

| Directory | Literal `exit(` | Literal `exit(1)` | Calls after lexical filtering | Of those, `exit(1)` |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `src/devices` | 263 | 241 | 135 | 132 |
| `src/cpus` | 112 | 94 | 74 | 74 |
| `src/machines` | 35 | 35 | 34 | 34 |
| **Total** | **410** | **370** | **243** | **240** |

The three additional executable calls are `dev_cons.c:80` (`exit(0)`, console halt), `dev_pmagja.c:223`, and `dev_px.c:811` (both `exit(2)`, initialization allocation failures).

The location classification, enumerated from those 243 positions, is:

| Population | Sites |
|---|---:|
| Runtime handlers and their helpers | **150** |
| Initialization/configuration: 41 device, 5 CPU, 34 machine sites | **80** |
| CPU generators and standalone experiment | **13** |
| **Total** | **243** |

Being inside a runtime function does not establish an outstanding guest-input defect. The 150 divide as follows:

| Runtime-function population | Sites |
|---|---:|
| Input-reachable error exits through enabled in-tree wiring | **98** |
| Dead/precluded paths, absent producers, or internal failures not established reachable | **33** |
| Optional instrumentation | **10** |
| Unattached or disabled device attachments | **6** |
| Intentional halt/reboot handling | **2** |
| Host-selected RAM configuration check misplaced in an access handler | **1** |
| **Total** | **150** |

The debugger is outside the earlier census scope. Its **three** additional sites are `debugger.c:223,883` and `debugger_expr.c:101`. Thus population **(b) is 80 within the original scope, or 83 including the debugger**; the corresponding expanded denominator is 246.

Tracker coverage is an overlay, not another disjoint population. I checked both [ledger.json](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/ledger.json) and [OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md).

| Owning row | State at HEAD | Covered physical sites |
|---|---|---|
| `n6` | held | Footbridge: **565,574,589,604,613,622,712,737** — eight live |
| `alphavmkill` | open | `memory_alpha.c:77` — one live |
